<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Molopo River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Molopo River is a mostly dry river of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> that rises near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahikeng">Mahikeng</a> and flows west towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a>. In 1885 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> made it the dividing line between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown colony</a> of British Bechuanaland to the south and the Bechuanaland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> to the north, and it still forms part of the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>.</p></div>
